  "question": "(a) By how much is the sum of $3\\frac{2}{3}$ and $2\\frac{1}{5}$ less than $7$?\n(b) The height, $h$ m, of a dock above sea level is given by $h = 6 + 4\\cos(15p)^\\circ$, $0 < p < 6$. Find: (i) the value of $h$ when $p = 4$; (ii) correct to two significant figures, the value of $p$ when $h = 9$ m.",
  "diagram": null,
  "options": [],
  "correctAnswer": -1,
  "explanation": "(a) $\\frac{11}{3} + \\frac{11}{5} = \\frac{88}{15}$. $7 - \\frac{88}{15} = \\frac{17}{15} = 1\\frac{2}{15}$.\n\n(b)(i) $h = 6 + 4\\cos 60^\\circ = 6 + 2 = 8$ m. (ii) $9 = 6 + 4\\cos(15p)^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\cos(15p)^\\circ = \\frac{3}{4} \\Rightarrow (15p)^\\circ = 41.4^\\circ \\Rightarrow p = 2.76 \\approx 2.8$ (2 s.f.).\n\n**Answers:** (a) $1\\frac{2}{15}$; (b)(i) $8$ m; (ii) $p \\approx 2.8$. (Match the printed key.)",
