  "section": "Section A",
  "type": "theory",
  "question": "A trapezium $PQRS$ is such that $PQ \\parallel RS$ and the perpendicular from $P$ to $RS$ is $40$ cm. If $|PQ| = 20$ cm, $|SP| = 50$ cm and $|SR| = 60$ cm, calculate, correct to 2 significant figures, the: (a) Area of the trapezium; (b) $\\angle QRS$.",
  "diagram": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 205\" width=\"270\" height=\"205\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\"><polygon points=\"20.0,170.0 230.0,170.0 195.0,30.0 125.0,30.0\" /><line x1=\"125.0\" y1=\"30.0\" x2=\"125.0\" y2=\"170.0\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><polyline points=\"133.0,170.0 133.0,162.0 125.0,162.0\" /><polyline points=\"153.8,33.3 160.0,30.0 153.8,26.7\" /><polyline points=\"113.8,173.3 120.0,170.0 113.8,166.7\" /><text x=\"119.0\" y=\"24.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >P</text><text x=\"201.0\" y=\"24.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >Q</text><text x=\"240.0\" y=\"174.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >R</text><text x=\"12.0\" y=\"174.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >S</text><text x=\"125.0\" y=\"186.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >T</text><text x=\"160.0\" y=\"24.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >20 cm</text><text x=\"121.0\" y=\"105.0\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >40 cm</text><text x=\"50.0\" y=\"100.0\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >50 cm</text><text x=\"125.0\" y=\"192.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\" >60 cm</text></svg>",
  "options": [],
  "correctAnswer": -1,
  "explanation": "(a) $A = \\frac{1}{2}(PQ + SR) \\times 40 = \\frac{1}{2}(20 + 60)(40) = 1600$ cm$^2$.\n\n(b) Let $T$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $P$ on $SR$ and $U$ the foot from $Q$. $|ST|^2 = 50^2 - 40^2 = 900 \\Rightarrow |ST| = 30$ cm. $|UR| = 60 - (30 + 20) = 10$ cm. $\\tan \\angle QRS = \\frac{40}{10} = 4 \\Rightarrow \\angle QRS = 75.96^\\circ \\approx 76^\\circ$.\n\n**Answers:** (a) $1600$ cm$^2$; (b) $76^\\circ$. (Match the printed key.)",
  "topic": "Mensuration and Trigonometry",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "solutionDiagram": null
